1.01 In this Agreement, the following terms shall have the meanings set out below, except as otherwise defined in the recitals or elsewhere in this Agreement:

"Benchmark" means any rate, index, or other value that is used to determine the amount payable under this Agreement;

"Benchmark Replacement" means the alternative to a Benchmark that is selected or determined in accordance with this Fallback Language;

"Benchmark Replacement Adjustment" means the amount, methodology, or other adjustment that is selected or determined in accordance with this Fallback Language;

"Benchmark Replacement Date" means the date on which a Benchmark Replacement is selected or determined in accordance with this Fallback Language;

"Benchmark Replacement Event" means the occurrence of any of the following events:

(a) a Benchmark is not available to be used for a period of five Business Days;

(b) a Benchmark is no longer published or a publication of a Benchmark is no longer publicly available;

(c) a regulatory body or a relevant administrator of a Benchmark determines that the Benchmark is no longer representative or appropriate for use; or

(d) any other event that, in the reasonable opinion of the Calculation Agent, makes the Benchmark unavailable or inappropriate for use;

"Calculation Agent" means [Calculation Agent Name], or such other Person as may be designated in accordance with this Agreement;

"Fallback Language" means this document, as may be amended or supplemented from time to time in accordance with this Agreement;

"Relevant Persons" means the parties to this Agreement and any other Person that is a party to an agreement that incorporates this Fallback Language by reference.

